  "body": "Bumps [omniauth](https://github.com/omniauth/omniauth) from 2.1.4 to 2.3.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/omniauth/omniauth/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md\">omniauth's changelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>[2.3.1] - 2026-10-22</h2>\n<h3>Fixed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><code>remember_sign_in</code> no longer raises <code>KeyError</code> when called outside the request phase, before <code>omniauth.params</code> is stored, as when a provider gem's specs call <code>authorize_params</code> directly.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>[2.3.0] - 2026-10-22</h2>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Let strategies keep the origin and params of several sign-ins in progress at once, for example in several tabs, so each callback gets its own instead of the latest sign-in's. A strategy opts in by calling <code>remember_sign_in</code> in its request phase with a value the provider sends back, such as OAuth 2.0's state, and overriding <code>callback_sign_in_key</code>. The latest 5 are stored in <code>session['omniauth.sign_ins']</code>, and <code>omniauth.origin</code> and <code>omniauth.params</code> still hold the latest one. See <a href=\"https://github.com/omniauth/omniauth/blob/master/README.md#several-sign-ins-at-once\">the README</a>. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/omniauth/omniauth-oauth2/issues/195\">omniauth-oauth2#195</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Changed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>The gem no longer includes <code>CHANGELOG.md</code>, which was about half its size. Its <code>changelog_uri</code> links to the changelog on GitHub.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>[2.2.0] - 2026-10-22</h2>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Add a <code>full_host</code> option for each strategy, as a string or a proc that takes the Rack env. It takes precedence over <code>OmniAuth.config.full_host</code>. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/omniauth/omniauth/issues/835\">#835</a>)</li>\n<li>Ship RBS type signatures for OmniAuth in <code>sig/</code>.</li>\n<li>Document the Rack env keys OmniAuth sets, CSRF protection, sending <code>origin</code> as a form field, and how <code>SameSite</code> session cookies affect the callback in the README. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/omniauth/omniauth/issues/909\">#909</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/omniauth/omniauth/pull/1075\">#1075</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/omniauth/omniauth/pull/1048\">#1048</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/omniauth/omniauth/issues/1149\">#1149</a>)</li>\n<li>Add this changelog.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Changed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><code>omniauth.params</code> now includes params posted to the request phase's form, not just its query string, so they survive the POST-only request phase introduced in 2.0. The <code>authenticity_token</code> param is never included (see CVE-2017-18076 under 1.3.2). If your request form posts other fields, they now appear in <code>omniauth.params</code> and are stored in the session until the callback. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/omniauth/omniauth/issues/975\">#975</a>)</li>\n<li><code>OmniAuth::Builder</code> builds its middleware stack on the first request and reuses it, instead of rebuilding every strategy on every request. Providers added after the first request are ignored. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/omniauth/omniauth/issues/1083\">#1083</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/omniauth/omniauth/issues/970\">#970</a>)</li>\n<li><code>Strategy#call</code> sends a request that isn't on the strategy's request or callback path straight to the app, instead of duplicating the strategy for it. It still duplicates it in test mode, with an <code>other_phase</code>, with path lambdas, or when the strategy overrides how <code>#call!</code> dispatches. Methods patched directly onto <code>OmniAuth::Strategy</code>, rather than overridden in a subclass, aren't detected, so a patched <code>#call!</code> no longer runs for requests outside the strategy's paths. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/omniauth/omniauth/pull/1172\">#1172</a>)</li>\n<li>Require Ruby 2.5 or later (was 2.2). (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/omniauth/omniauth/pull/1167\">#1167</a>)</li>\n<li>Require Rack 2.2.8 or later (was 2.2.3), rack-protection 2.2.0 or later, and hashie 3.5.2 or later (was 3.4.6).</li>\n<li>The gem now contains only <code>lib</code>, <code>sig</code>, the license, the README, the changelog, and the security policy.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Fixed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Run the <code>before_callback_phase</code> hook for mocked failures in test mode, as for real callbacks. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/omniauth/omniauth/issues/1043\">#1043</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/omniauth/omniauth/pull/1171\">#1171</a>)</li>\n<li>Recognize callback paths with a format suffix, such as <code>/auth/:provider/callback.json</code>. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/omniauth/omniauth/issues/618\">#618</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/omniauth/omniauth/pull/1170\">#1170</a>)</li>\n<li>Don't fail callbacks when the app defines a method named <code>uid</code>, <code>info</code>, <code>credentials</code>, or <code>extra</code> on <code>Object</code>. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/omniauth/omniauth/issues/898\">#898</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/omniauth/omniauth/pull/1169\">#1169</a>)</li>\n<li>Don't add a calculated <code>name</code> to the info hash subsets returned by <code>slice</code>, <code>except</code>, <code>select</code>, and <code>reject</code>. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/omniauth/omniauth/issues/892\">#892</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/omniauth/omniauth/pull/1168\">#1168</a>)</li>\n<li>Collapse repeated slashes in the request path, as Rails routing does, so <code>//auth/:provider</code> from a misconfigured proxy reaches the strategy. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/omniauth/omniauth/issues/1079\">#1079</a>)</li>\n<li>Avoid &quot;instance variable not initialized&quot; warnings on Ruby before 3.0.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Security</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Guard against forged hosts in callback URLs. Unless a <code>full_host</code> is set, OmniAuth builds the callback URL it sends to the provider from the request's <code>Host</code>, <code>X-Forwarded-Host</code>, or <code>Forwarded</code> header, which a client can forge. The new <code>OmniAuth.config.allowed_hosts</code>, a list of strings and regexps, makes the request and callback phases fail with <code>invalid_host</code> unless the request's host matches one of them. Until <code>full_host</code> or <code>allowed_hosts</code> is set, the request phase logs a warning. The README's <code>full_host</code> example, which copied the <code>Host</code> header, is fixed. (<a href=\"https://github.com/omniauth/omniauth/security/advisories/GHSA-m27g-v28p-f9fx\">GHSA-m27g-v28p-f9fx</a>, CVE-2026-63183)</li>\n<li>Run <code>request_validation_phase</code> before writing <code>omniauth.params</code> to the session, so a cross-site POST rejected by the authenticity check can no longer store attacker-controlled params. (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/omniauth/omniauth/pull/1162\">#1162</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/omniauth/omniauth/commit/58138036a8f543a7ffa5c896c82e155f06e33e08\"><code>5813803</code></a> Release 2.3.1</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/omniauth/omniauth/commit/dde1f8692dbaf753803be39c826bb1da8acb3aa8\"><code>dde1f86</code></a> Let remember_sign_in run before omniauth.params is stored</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/omniauth/omniauth/commit/9db25e18630f0eeed12b2064bc09dfc323f5bb5d\"><code>9db25e1</code></a> Release 2.3.0</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/omniauth/omniauth/commit/d9f73a020f3135b44c683b56bf3064731f693c99\"><code>d9f73a0</code></a> Require json in the sign-ins spec</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/omniauth/omniauth/commit/4905b9010473f824771f23f9053d9e263581569f\"><code>4905b90</code></a> Let strategies keep several sign-ins' origins apart</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/omniauth/omniauth/commit/8dc4b1ef663f8c8c44b65b4655f920d07622f48d\"><code>8dc4b1e</code></a> Stop shipping CHANGELOG.md in the gem</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/omniauth/omniauth/commit/474bc91c12619218f15eeb80bb30d1d66ea96c87\"><code>474bc91</code></a> Make rake release tag and push without pushing the gem</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/omniauth/omniauth/commit/0d3807816151b08da1a84b600f0260d83d2f4aee\"><code>0d38078</code></a> Release 2.2.0</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/omniauth/omniauth/commit/943b44faea242f063fa9230254fe7d60cfcc9c90\"><code>943b44f</code></a> Add allowed_hosts to guard against forged hosts</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/omniauth/omniauth/commit/a241c941c86dd7c4133b3e64f0aad15cc14feae6\"><code>a241c94</code></a> Make the shipped signatures loadable from other gems</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/omniauth/omniauth/compare/v2.1.4...v2.3.1\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility score](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=omniauth&package-manager=bundler&previous-version=2.1.4&new-version=2.3.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't alter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting `@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits that have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n\n\n</details>",
